  "report_period": "Week 23 (30th May to 6th Jun 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Nissen Kaiun have committed their Mini Cape \"Bastions\" 119/2011 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026, Scrubber fitted) at region USD 16,5 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Brilliant Jupiter\" 119/2010 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 07/2025) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 16 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Shun Fu Da\" 82/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) of Eastern Fortune Shipping was committed to Indian interests at USD 11,4 mill. Note that back in April, the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Seaduty\" 82/2008 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 04/2026, DD 11/2025) was sold at USD 14,25 mill. Pavimar have committed their Panamax \"Toro\" 76/2008 Imabari, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 10/2025) at USD 12,2 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Aeolian Grace\" 76/2007 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2027, DD 11/2025) was sold at USD 11,2 mill. On the Supramax sector, Oskar Wehr committed their \"Ingwar Selmer\" 58/2011 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 03/2026) at USD 11,7 mill, while the \"Incredible Blue\" 57/2011 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 10/2026) from Load Line Marine was committed at high USD 11 mill. Moreover, the \"Annita\" 53/2005 New Century, China (SS 11/2027, DD 10/2025) of Z&G Halcoussis was committed at USD 8,5 mill, the same price achieved a couple of weeks ago for the \"Spar Virgo\" 53/2005 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 06/2025). The Handysize \"Sider Olympia\" 38/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 06/2027, DD 09/2025, Semi boxed) was committed to Greek interests at region USD 15,75 mill. For reference, the two-years-younger \"Unity Star\" 37/2015 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 08/2025, Semi boxed) was sold a month ago at USD 18,25 mill. In addition, ID Management committed the \"ID Pioneer\" 35/2012 Taizhou, China (SS 11/2027, DD 11/2025) to Chinese interests at USD 10,1 mill. Note that the \"Celeste\" 34/2012 Zhejiang, China (SS/DD 02/2027) was sold in May at USD 11 mill.",
    "tankers": "The MR2 sister vessels \"Clearocean Maria\" & \"Clearocean Mary\" 50/2014 Spp, Korea (SS 08/2029, DD 07/2027 & SS 10/2029, DD 01/2028) were committed to undisclosed interests at USD 29,5 mill each. Remind you that a couple of weeks ago, the \"STI Regina\" 50/2014 Spp, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 09/2027, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 31 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 9,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 8,000/10,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 6,000/9,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. West African trips via North Coast South America into Continent were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 300K/500K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 11,750 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 13,000 pd basis delivery China for 1 year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Indian trips into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 5,000/7,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Continental trips via Baltic into India were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into US East Coast were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 160K. Trips from Black Sea into Arabian Gulf were reported at the level of usd 11,000/12,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from Japan into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 13,000/15,000 pd range. Indian coastal trips were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Inter-Continent were reported at the level of usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips via Continent were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. US Gulf coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 16,000/17,000 pd. South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A large Handysize was fixed on a period at the usd 12,650 pd basis delivery Caribbean for 5/7 months employment with redelivery Singapore/Japan range."
    }
  },
